## Executive Summary

The strongest validated components of this opportunity are: (1) **improved revenue forecasting accuracy**, where LTS's 2025 budget assumed a smooth $4.34M–$6.63M monthly revenue curve while actual results ranged from $1.96M to $9.52M [3]; (2) **equipment acquisition timing optimization**, directly relevant as LTS evaluates a fourth stacker purchase with 100% fleet utilization [4]; and (3) **bid accuracy improvement**, where Neil Sanders identifies an inability to explain why the same repeat client yields 70% margin one year and 55% the next [5]. A conservative, validated estimate for combined annual EBITDA impact is **$0.595M–$1.28M**, with implementation costs of **$63.8K–$170K** and a 6–12 month time-to-value.

