### Projected Impact

#### Reframing the Opportunity: Three Distinct Value Streams

The most defensible component. LTS's 2025 budget assumed smooth monthly revenue but actual results showed $1.96M–$9.52M swings, producing a cumulative EBITDA miss of −$2.41M [3]. Better forecasting would not change the revenue itself, but it would enable:

#### Consolidated Impact Assessment

| Value Stream | Annual EBITDA Impact | Confidence | Time to Value |
|---|---|---|---|
| Revenue Forecast Accuracy & Cash Flow | $170K–$425K | High | 3–6 months |
| Bid Accuracy & Margin Optimization | $255K–$510K | Medium | 6–12 months |
| Demand Shaping & Project Sequencing | $170K–$340K | Low–Medium | 9–18 months |
| **Total Estimated Impact** | **$595K–$1,280K** | **Medium** | **6–12 months (blended)** |

On LTS's 2025 EBITDA of $24.2M, this represents **2.5%–5.3% EBITDA improvement** [1]. Against the 2026 budget-implied Adjusted EBITDA of $30.1M [3], it represents **2.0%–4.2%**. Against the 2026 LTS-only budget of $65.8M revenue with $30.1M Adjusted EBITDA [22], the EBITDA margin impact is approximately **0.9–1.9 percentage points**.

#### Payback Period and ROI

| Phase | Scope | Estimated Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Discovery & Data Readiness | Data inventory, schema, quality | $4.25K–$21.2K |
| Model Development & Validation | Custom forecasting models, backtesting | $21.2K–$85K |
| Deployment & Integration | MLOps, integration with existing tools | $10.6K–$35.3K |
| Ongoing Annual (cloud + maintenance) | Inference, retraining, monitoring | $7.1K–$21.2K/year |

